  "notes": "An intransitive verb describing the gradual bending or sagging of something under load. Can also be written in kanji as {撓|たわ}む, though the kana form is more common. Conjugation: たわまない, たわみます, たわむ, たわめば, たわんだ (note the んだ past form typical of む-ending verbs).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {枝|えだ}がたわむ — a branch bends (under fruit/snow)\n- {棚|たな}がたわむ — a shelf sags (under books/weight)\n- {重|おも}みでたわむ — to sag under the weight\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- たわめる — to bend something (transitive counterpart)\n- {曲|ま}がる — to bend, to curve (more general; includes turning)\n- しなる — to flex, to bend elastically (implies springiness)",
